  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2020) position from Islami Bank Bangladesh's own audited annual report 'Five Years Performance' table, taken from the FY2021 report. SOLO / STANDALONE basis. Islami Bank Bangladesh is a Shariah-compliant bank, so its own terminology is used in original_metric_name: 'Investment' is the financing book (the equivalent of loans and advances), 'Investment Income' is the equivalent of interest income, and 'Profit Paid on deposit' is the equivalent of interest expense. The normalised metric names map these onto the dataset's conventional banking vocabulary: gross_loans holds General Investment, net_interest_income holds Net Investment Income, and classified_loans holds Classified Investment. Total liabilities are calculated as total assets (excluding contra) minus shareholders' equity; the source table does not print a total-liabilities line. total_assets is the balance-sheet total EXCLUDING contra items, which is the comparable figure for other banks in this dataset; the bank's own 'Total Assets (including Contra)' is retained separately as total_assets_incl_contra and is materially larger. The FY2020 annual report is a scanned document whose text layer is unusable (its cover renders as mojibake and no table row survives extraction), so this year is taken from the FY2021 report's comparative column. RESTATEMENTS -- 2 figure(s) in this record are reported differently by other Islami Bank annual reports. Per this dataset's sourcing rule the contemporaneous value is kept and the divergence recorded here: provision_classified: this record uses 23572 (AR2021); AR2022/AR2024 report 12725.9; provision_required_classified: this record uses 23572 (AR2021); AR2024 report 12725.9.",
